WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.785
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit 6: People in Society.

2
00:00:03.865 --> 00:00:11.013
Unit 6 is about the people who keep a community
working: the helpers, the leaders, and the newcomers.

3
00:00:11.093 --> 00:00:19.530
You will meet a caretaker, a carpenter, an engineer and a
merchant, then governors, senators, lawyers and the military,

4
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:26.115
and finally artists, photographers, messengers,
refugees, immigrants, tenants and consumers.

5
00:00:26.195 --> 00:00:33.701
You will use the Present Simple to say what each person
does, should and mustn't to give advice and rules,

6
00:00:33.781 --> 00:00:39.498
prepositions to say where people go, and
the past tenses to retell what happened.

7
00:00:39.578 --> 00:00:47.586
By the end you will describe the helpers in your own town,
just as Amal does in the story “The Community Parade”.

8
00:00:47.666 --> 00:00:53.598
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:53.678 --> 00:00:55.522
By the end of this unit,

10
00:00:55.602 --> 00:01:03.300
you will be able to name and describe at least
twenty jobs and roles that people play in society.

11
00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:10.196
You will also explain what different workers
and leaders do, using the Present Simple.

12
00:01:10.276 --> 00:01:15.568
You will also give advice and state
rules using should and mustn't.

13
00:01:15.648 --> 00:01:18.535
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:18.615 --> 00:01:25.201
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: caretaker,
carpenter, labourer, engineer, merchant, governor.

15
00:01:25.281 --> 00:01:30.248
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:30.328 --> 00:01:34.173
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:34.253 --> 00:01:40.650
The reading sequence includes The People of Our
Town and Two Neighbours: A Refugee and an Immigrant.

18
00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:41.556
Read actively.

19
00:01:41.636 --> 00:01:46.025
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

20
00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:50.234
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

21
00:01:50.314 --> 00:01:54.769
The first language focus is Present
Simple: describing everyday jobs.

22
00:01:54.849 --> 00:02:00.421
We use the Present Simple for routines,
facts, and things that happen again and again.

23
00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:07.585
It suits jobs perfectly, because most jobs repeat every
day: “The caretaker cleans the school every morning.”

24
00:02:07.665 --> 00:02:14.749
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

25
00:02:14.829 --> 00:02:18.710
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1: Describe a Job.

26
00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:23.285
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

27
00:02:23.365 --> 00:02:26.768
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

28
00:02:26.848 --> 00:02:30.387
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

29
00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:32.070
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:39.315
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

31
00:02:39.395 --> 00:02:42.828
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

32
00:02:42.908 --> 00:02:51.098
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
